# METHODOLOGICAL INFORMATION\
\
## Description of methods used for collection/generation of data:\
- PRISM annual mean temperature data downloaded using the prism R package\
- Population raster obtained from Gridded Population of the World, Version 4 (GPWv4): Population Count, Revision 11 (CIESIN, Columbia University; 2010, 2.5 arc-minute)\
- County polygons obtained from US Census shapefiles (2010 Cartographic Boundary File, 1:20,000,000; Alaska, Hawaii and Puerto Rico removed)\
- County-level anomalies calculated relative to the 1960\'961980 baseline\
\
## Methods for processing the data:\
- Raster data were aligned with county polygons\
- Population-weighted aggregation performed using a sparse matrix\
- Baseline means computed and subtracted to calculate anomalies\
- Visualizations created using R base plotting functions and RColorBrewer for color scales\
- GIF animation created using magick package\
\
## Instrument- or software-specific information needed to interpret the data:\
- R version 4.x or higher\
- Required packages: sf, terra, RColorBrewer, Matrix, tmaptools, prism, parallel, magick\
\
* Standards and calibration information, if appropriate: PRISM temperature data calibrated according to PRISM Climate Group standards\
* Environmental/experimental conditions: Data represent historical climate conditions; no experimental interventions\
* Describe any quality-assurance procedures performed on the data: Counties with missing raster values excluded; population-weighted aggregation ensures consistency\
* People involved with sample collection, processing, analysis and/or submission: N/A (data processing, analysis, visualization)\
